{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.VertexOperator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.VertexOperator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.FiberBundle.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Circle"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ope_is_skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ope_is_skein","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-operator.lean#L76-L107","doc":"The OPE of any two vertex operators has its leading singularity\nrecorded by the Hecke eigenvalue pair: bosonic `q`, fermionic\n`-q⁻¹`, from `(T - q)(T + q⁻¹) = 0` — the Skein relation\n`L₊ - L₋ = (q - q⁻¹)L₀` applied to the strand collision on `𝒮_p`.\n\n**This was a bare `axiom`, and what it asserts is weaker than it\nreads. Both facts are stated here rather than left to be\nrediscovered.**\n\nIt was an `axiom`, so it polluted `#print axioms` for every\ndownstream statement (§\"Axiomatization is NOT a Proof\"). It is now\na theorem, and the proof is `⟨⟨Y₁, Y₂, q, -q_inv_param⟩, rfl, rfl,\nrfl, rfl⟩` — because `OPE` is a plain record with the eigenvalues\nas *fields*, so exhibiting one with those values is record\nconstruction, not mathematics. Assuming it bought nothing.\n\nSo what is **established**: an `OPE` carrying the Hecke pair exists\nfor any two operators. What is **not**: that the pair is *forced*.\nThat needs the Hecke generator acting on the collision and its\nquadratic relation — i.e. `OPE` would have to carry the action and\nderive the eigenvalues, rather than take them as data. Until then\nthe values `q` and `-q⁻¹` are put in by hand and this theorem\ncannot tell a right pair from a wrong one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OPE.fermionic_eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OPE.fermionic_eigenvalue","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-operator.lean#L74-L74","doc":"The antisymmetric (fermionic) eigenvalue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OPE.bosonic_eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OPE.bosonic_eigenvalue","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-operator.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The symmetric (bosonic) eigenvalue of the Hecke generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OPE.right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OPE.right","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-operator.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OPE.left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OPE.left","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-operator.lean#L69-L69","doc":"The two vertex operators whose collision is being resolved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OPE.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OPE.mk","kind":"ctor","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-operator.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OPE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OPE","kind":"structure","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-operator.lean#L64-L74","doc":"The OPE (operator product expansion) of two vertex operators.\nRecords the leading singularity data: the eigenvalues of the\nHecke generator T acting on the collision Y₁(z)Y₂(w) as z → w. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexOperator.weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexOperator.weight","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-operator.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Conformal weight (jet level) of the state. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexOperator.bundle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexOperator.bundle","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-operator.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The base space for the insertion — the Reeb bundle `ℛ_p`.\n\n**Carried as a type parameter `B`, not as `ReebBundle q`, and the\nreason is a layer wall rather than a missing import.**\n`def:reeb-bundle` is `structure ReebBundle (q : ℝ)` — an\n*archimedean* object (its `substrate` field is `q > 1`, its\n`holonomy` is a `Real.exp`), and its own header says \"NOT part of\nthe formal proof chain\". This file is over the categorical ground\nring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`. Writing `ReebBundle q` here is therefore\nnot just unreachable (a content-block sibling cannot import a\nsibling — they sit outside the Lake globs) but **type-wrong**: it\napplies an ℝ-indexed structure to a Laurent polynomial, which is\nthe §7c straddle the ground-ring convention exists to prevent.\n\nParameterising keeps the vertex-operator algebra on the\ncategorical side. An archimedean consumer instantiates\n`B := ReebBundle q₀` after the τ functor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexOperator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexOperator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-operator.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VertexOperator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VertexOperator","kind":"structure","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-operator.lean#L37-L62","doc":"A vertex operator on the exceptional divisor 𝒮_p.\nGiven a state a ∈ V_n (level n of the brane tower), the vertex\noperator Y(a, z) is a formal Laurent series in the affine\ncoordinate z = v₁/v₂ on 𝒮_p whose modes are R-matrix insertions. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:vertex-operator","label":"def:vertex-operator","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-operator.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-operator.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-operator.lean#L34-L34","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-operator.lean#L31-L33","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}